'' SELECT CASE AS CONST over an integer subject whose cases are all constants it holds is
'' ONE LLVM 'switch' (mir/lowerswitch.tiko), which clang makes a lookup or jump table as it
'' does fbc's own. Anything else keeps the compare chain. Expected output is fbc-modern 1.20's
'' for the same program: the switch's answers -- ranges, signed and unsigned subjects at
'' every width, a character through a pointer, exit select, nesting, a string local across
'' a return, the int64 extremes -- and the chain's, where a case value is outside what the
'' subject holds and fbc compares in the promoted type.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -O2 tests/codegen/src/select-const-switch.bas -o tests/codegen/selectconstswitch.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/selectconstswitch.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  10 20 99
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 2 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 2 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 2 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 2 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 2 2 3 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 1 2 3 4
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  303
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 20 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: local1 local2 local
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 3 4 4
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1 2 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: t
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: else
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: else
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: m1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: else
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: else
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: big
